It is DNS that causes this behaviour. telnetd is trying to translate the
incoming connections ip address back to a name, the delay is the DNS timing
out.
    Just to test edit /etc/svc.conf and change hosts=local,bind to
hosts=local Then verify that the DNS server listed in /etc/resolv.conf is
valid and answering your queries and make sure its answering reverse lookups
for your ip address ranges esp the one matching the slow connect PC.

    Now you even said "it may have something to do with DNS" why don't you
verify your DNS config! I was happy with you till you admitted you knew what
was at fault and you had not looked there first!

    Anyway that should kick your brain into gear


