"official" way.

Boot the distribution CD:



##############################################################################
##
  ##  Saving system hardware configuration from dsk0 . . . Done.
##
##############################################################################


*** Performing CDROM Installation

^C

# fsck /dev/rdisk/dsk0a
/sbin/ufs_fsck /dev/rdisk/dsk0a
** /dev/rdisk/dsk0a
** Last Mounted on /
** Phase 1 - Check Blocks and Sizes
** Phase 2 - Check Pathnames# mount /dev/disk/dsk0a /mnt
** Phase 3 - Check Connectivity
** Phase 4 - Check Reference Counts
** Phase 5 - Check Cyl groups

#mount /dev/disk/dsk0a /mnt


and.... you're there.

