Following is the complete response I got to the same question a couple 
years ago. Using gdb-4.17 the patch that Norbert sent me works quite well
(at least on pre-5.1 releases of Tru64).


******starts here****


Hi Jim,

>... if you would be willing ...
Of course, appended is the patch to make gdb work with code
generated by egcs-1.1.x. The patch applies to stock gdb-4.17
as it can be found at every GNU mirror.

>... that gdb-4.18 would fix the problem ...
No, not at all. It seems to me that gdb-4.18 has some other
serious bugs. (Didn't get the time to dig into it).


Actually there are two bugs. A big one in egcs-1.1.x and small
one in gdb-4.17. The patch fixes the small bug in gdb and it
contains a work around for the big egcs bug. A real egcs bug
fix would not only affect the machine dependend parts of egcs
but it would also affect some machine independend parts of it.
Unfortunately I do not have the time to fix it. So I contacted
the egcs maintainer and he asserted me that my request got queued.
For that chances are good to get a working egcs in a couple of
years ;-). Anyway, here is the patch. It would be nice to hear
from you if it works.


Best regards,
-- 
Norbert


