Hello,

  I think this problem is answered in the release notes from the C++
compiler. It's because some of the STD symbols are in a static library at
the moment, so when you link,  some of these symbols are added to your .so
files, and when finally linking, the symbols happen to be defined in
several object files. There is a workaround for this problem explained in
the release notes (at least for V6.1), but it's not enough, as I did still
have problems. I had to put the '-hidden xxx' statement exactly between the
object files and the shared libraries I linked them with. Maybe this has
changed a little in more recent versions though.

  Regards,

    Jeremie Petit

