processor Ultra 90; a single processor HP c3600 (392 CFP2000) would beat
a single processor SunBlade and a single processor Alpha 21264(x) (514
CFP2000@EV67/667 Mhz, 590 CFP2000@EV68/833Mhz) would beat all of the
above (www.spec.org).  And if you like SMP you'll love either the DS20
or the ES40 !!  Heck, my "old" EV6/500 ES40 chews up MatLab models
better than anything else we have benchmarked.

If you want to crunch (floating point) numbers there is still nothing
faster than an Alpha !!  Why do you think all of the Human Genome
Project folks have been using them almost exclusively for the past
couple of years !!!


