francois reygagne <freygagne@opteway.com> writes:

>Could anyone help me. I want to make tcp rejected my incoming request
>when the tcp listen queue is full on Linux, Solaris 2.8, Tru64, HP-UX and AIX.



You cannot do so on Solaris; you cannot do so using the socket interface.

"Connection refused"  is not for cases when queues are full.  Instead,
common practice is to drop the SYN on the floor.

To the client "Connection Refused" means: oh, no listener.  Let's not retry.
(Unless you use Windows which is broken in this regard)

Casper
