estratosfera@my-deja.com wrote:
> 
> Hello, I have to install a machine which has two hard disks so I would
> like to install one swap area in each disk because I have heard that
> the system will work faster than a system with only one swap area.

Most Unix systems (certainly BSD), including Tru64, stripe I/O when more
than one swap device is available.  So, swap data is evenly distributed
across all available swap partitions.  Performance gains can be realized
using multiple partitions (especially when the disks are attached to
separate controllers) due to reduced head seek times.

Tony V.
Kernel Group


