Perhaps I am again misunderstanding you.
On your X server (Exceed) you can make three types of XDMCP connections:  
Query, Broadcast, or Indirect.
You should be using query, not broadcast.  Because you already know the 
name of the Tru64 server you want to login to.

If your goal is to login to your DEC box, using a Windows machine as your X 
terminal, and you want to use the CDE environment, here's what you should 
do:

Set up Exceed to use an XDMCP (or XDM) query to the IP address (or network 
name) of your DEC box.  I suggest using Single window mode, not multiple 
window mode.  (Perhaps there's no choice, I'm not sure.)

When you launch exceed in this configuration, you should be presented with 
the graphical login screen just like you'd expect if you were sitting at 
the local graphics terminal and keyboard.  It's important to note two 
things:  Your password is not encrypted as it goes through the network, and 
you can't login as root without modifying /etc/securettys


