Use the C++ compiler to link:

cc -c -I../cpplib  ctest.c
cxx -o ctest ctest.o  -L../cpplib/ -lcpplib

Make sure that the template instantiations present in cxx_repository
are put into the libcpp.a archive, alternatively you can create a
shared library using the command "cxx -shared -o libcpplib.so <object
files>";
This will automatically put all the instantiations in the shared
library. You did not get this problem when you used :string" because, the
instantiation of template basic_string<char> is present in libcxx.so. You
can verify that you will get linker errors with your original version if you
had compiled all you C++ files with -D__FORCE_INSTANTIATIONS.
Check the C++ headers for details on this.

Hope this helps.

rajanish...




