This is fairly standard UNIX speak for "oops, it didn't work".  The
other way UNIX likes to say this is "bus error, core dumped".

Not terribly specific messages, but the core file is the key.  It can be
used by a programmer with a debugger to figure out what went wrong inside
the program.  The number of possibilities is immense.

If the application is something written in house, gte in contact with
the group which provides it.  If it's something you bought get in
contact with the vendor.  They are likely to need the core dump file and
may need some of the input data your user is running with.

