For a treatment of memory barriers etc, read Unix for multiprocessors
by Curt Schimmel. Any decent pthread programming book should
talk about it: E.g. Programming Posix threads by D Butenhof.
The books explain why they are required. Also check out
Sun Multi-threaded programming guide on Sun web site. You
can do a search for it.

pthread calls like mutex_lock(), mutex_unlock(), pthread_create()
etc., introduce memory barriers, and normally an application
programmers do not need to worry about it, since the
mechanisms differ from platform to platform.

