In article <3A548425.2E4007A3@minbar.zko.dec.com>, Daniel Christians <danielc@minbar.zko.dec.com> writes:
> hi,
> 
> is there a doc, or can someone explain why a
> a user application program which uses pthreads 
> (DECthreads) would need to use the memory barrier
> instruction? (or alternatively the wmb instruction).
> the application happens to be the java vm.
> 

IIRC DECthreads can run threads simultaneously on different CPUs in an
SMP machine.  The only way one thread can know that another thread sees
a consistent set of data is via a memory barrier.

On a single CPU system the memory barrier is only really needed when
passing data off to an external device (all Alphas always need to work
like multi-processor machines due to this).  The code in DECthreads is
probably generic and does the MB's any time data could be passed from
thread to thread.

