>
> int
> main()
> {
>         for ( int i = 0 ; i < 100 ; i++ ) { foo() ; }
>         return 0 ;
> }
> -------------------------------------------------------
>
> I compiled the program as follows:
> cxx -g -pthread hp.cc -o hp
>
> I tried to profile it as follows:
> atom hp  -tool hiprof -env threads \
>      -toolargs="-textout -cputime -threads" -all -g
>
> When I run hp.hiprof.threads, I get the following message:
> Hiprof Panic: hacked stack back to nothing
>
> I do not understand what I am doing wrong, when the "threads"
> option is not specified during profile and compilation time
