First of all, uerf is very old and won't dig anything out of the system
for you.  DECevent is the replacement and will deliver far more
information.  The binary is "dia" and the arguments you give it are
similar to those for uerf.

Second, what are you seeing for a system load?  CPU saturation?  Paging
and/or swapping; memory utilization?

Third, how does the system behave when you're connected via the console?

Fourth, how do rlogin and ftp behave?  Do they show the same symptoms?

Fifth, what's going on with other systems in the LAN (which appears to
be non-switched since you mentioned "hub")?  Possibly a NIC in a system
somewhere that's decided to vomit stuff all over the LAN segment (whose
boundaries are probably defined by "next switch" or "next router")?
Streaming video running somewhere?  Someone left "ping -f" running?  If
there are activity lights on the hub(s), what do they tell you?

That's how I'd attack this one.

WJD


